# Product Requirements Document: Redis + MongoDB Caching Architecture
**Date:** November 21, 2025
**Version:** 1.0
**Author:** System Architect
**Project:** AdSyntheX - Dual-Layer Caching System

---

## Executive Summary

This document outlines the implementation of a **dual-layer caching architecture** combining Redis (hot cache) and MongoDB (warm/persistent storage) to solve data inconsistency issues, improve dashboard load times, and handle historical data queries efficiently.

### Current Problems
1. ❌ **Data Inconsistency**: Individual account totals don't match overall totals
2. ❌ **Slow Historical Queries**: Custom date ranges take 30-60 seconds
3. ❌ **No Data Persistence**: Redis-only cache expires, requiring repeated API calls
4. ❌ **Failed MongoDB Syncs**: Previous implementation had timeout and connection issues
5. ❌ **Rate Limit Concerns**: 10k daily Google Ads API quota with 83 accounts

### Solution Overview
- **Redis Cache**: 15-minute TTL for hot data (today/yesterday)
- **MongoDB Storage**: Permanent storage for all historical data
- **Smart Querying**: Automatic routing to fastest data source
- **Reliable Syncing**: 15-minute cron job with error handling
- **Data Consistency**: Verify totals by querying MongoDB aggregations

---

## Architecture Overview

### Three-Tier Data Flow

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  TIER 1: REDIS CACHE (Hot Data - Last 2 days)                   │
│  • TTL: 15 minutes                                               │
│  • Size: ~50-100 MB                                              │
│  • Hit Rate: 85-95% (most users view today)                      │
│  • Load Time: 50-100ms                                           │
└─────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
              │ Cache Miss
              ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  TIER 2: MONGODB (Warm Data - All Historical)                   │
│  • TTL: Permanent                                                │
│  • Size: ~500 MB (90 days) - grows over time                     │
│  • Hit Rate: 10-15% (historical queries)                         │
│  • Load Time: 200-500ms (indexed queries)                        │
└─────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
              │ Data Not Found
              ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  TIER 3: LIVE API (Cold Data - Never Synced)                    │
│  • TTL: N/A (live fetch)                                         │
│  • Hit Rate: <1% (very old or custom ranges)                     │
│  • Load Time: 30-60 seconds                                      │
│  • After fetch: Save to MongoDB for future queries               │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

---

## MongoDB Schema Design

### Database Structure

**Database Name:** `adsynthex`

**Collections (9 total):**

| Collection Name | Purpose | Size Estimate | Indexes |
|----------------|---------|---------------|---------|
| `afs_cost` | Google Ads cost data for AFS accounts | 50 MB/month | 3 |
| `afs_revenue` | AdSense revenue data by style_id | 30 MB/month | 3 |
| `compado_cost` | Google Ads cost for Compado accounts | 40 MB/month | 3 |
| `compado_revenue` | Compado conversions data | 20 MB/month | 3 |
| `adscom_cost` | Google Ads cost for Ads.com accounts | 80 MB/month | 3 |
| `adscom_revenue` | Ads.com article performance data | 40 MB/month | 2 |
| `sync_status` | Track sync status per account/feed | <1 MB | 2 |
| `sync_history` | Audit log of all sync operations | 10 MB/year | 2 |
| `data_snapshots` | Daily aggregated snapshots for reports | 5 MB/month | 2 |

**Total Storage:** ~260 MB/month × 3 months retention = **~780 MB**
**MongoDB Atlas Free Tier:** 512 MB ❌ **Need paid tier ($9/month for 2GB)**

---

### Collection Schemas

#### 1. Cost Collections (afs_cost, compado_cost, adscom_cost)

```typescript
interface CostDocument {
  _id: ObjectId;

  // Account & Campaign Info
  account_id: string;           // Google Ads account ID
  campaign_id: string;
  campaign_name: string;
  ad_group_id?: string;
  ad_group_name?: string;
  ad_id?: string;
  ad_name?: string;

  // Date
  date: string;                 // YYYY-MM-DD format

  // Cost Metrics
  cost_micros: number;          // Cost in micros ($1.50 = 1500000)
  clicks: number;
  impressions: number;
  conversions: number;
  ctr: number;
  cpc: number;

  // Feed-Specific Matching Keys
  style_id?: string;            // AFS only
  domain?: string;              // AFS only
  gclid?: string;               // Compado only
  article?: string;             // Ads.com only

  // Metadata
  feed_type: 'afs' | 'compado' | 'adscom';
  created_at: Date;
  updated_at: Date;
}
```

**Indexes:**
```javascript
// Unique constraint to prevent duplicates
db.afs_cost.createIndex(
  { account_id: 1, date: 1, style_id: 1, campaign_id: 1 },
  { unique: true, name: 'unique_cost_entry' }
);

// Query performance indexes
db.afs_cost.createIndex(
  { date: 1, feed_type: 1 },
  { name: 'date_feed_lookup' }
);

db.afs_cost.createIndex(
  { style_id: 1, date: 1 },
  { name: 'style_date_lookup', sparse: true }  // Sparse for AFS only
);
```

#### 2. Revenue Collections (afs_revenue, compado_revenue, adscom_revenue)

```typescript
interface RevenueDocument {
  _id: ObjectId;

  // Revenue Metrics
  revenue_usd: number;
  revenue_eur: number;
  clicks: number;
  impressions: number;
  date: string;

  // Feed-Specific Matching Keys
  style_id?: string;            // AFS
  domain?: string;              // AFS
  country_name?: string;        // AFS
  gclid?: string;               // Compado
  article?: string;             // Ads.com

  // Feed-Specific Metrics
  // AFS: country_name
  // Compado: conversion_type, device, country, traffic_source
  // Ads.com: visits, ctr, rpm, epc, ivt_correction, finalized

  // Metadata
  feed_type: 'afs' | 'compado' | 'adscom';
  created_at: Date;
  updated_at: Date;
}
```

**Indexes:**
```javascript
db.afs_revenue.createIndex(
  { style_id: 1, date: 1 },
  { unique: true, name: 'unique_revenue_entry', sparse: true }
);

db.afs_revenue.createIndex(
  { date: 1, feed_type: 1 },
  { name: 'date_feed_lookup' }
);
```

#### 3. Sync Status Collection

```typescript
interface SyncStatusDocument {
  _id: ObjectId;
  feed_type: 'afs' | 'compado' | 'adscom';
  account_id: string;
  last_sync_date: string;       // Last date successfully synced
  last_sync_time: Date;
  status: 'success' | 'failed' | 'in_progress' | 'skipped';
  error_message?: string;
  records_synced: number;
  duration_ms: number;
  updated_at: Date;
}
```

**Indexes:**
```javascript
db.sync_status.createIndex(
  { feed_type: 1, account_id: 1 },
  { unique: true, name: 'unique_sync_status' }
);

db.sync_status.createIndex(
  { last_sync_time: -1 },
  { name: 'recent_syncs' }
);
```

