## Cron Sync Worker Design

### Worker Configuration

**File:** `scripts/mongodb-sync-worker.js`

**Execution:**
- **Interval:** Every 15 minutes
- **Timeout:** 10 minutes max (per sync cycle)
- **Deployment:** Render Background Worker
- **Health Check:** HTTP endpoint on port 10000

### Sync Flow

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  STEP 1: Initialize (5 seconds)                                  │
│  • Connect to MongoDB (connection pool)                          │
│  • Connect to Redis                                              │
│  • Verify environment variables                                  │
└─────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
              ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  STEP 2: Fetch Cost Data (2-4 minutes)                          │
│  • Batch accounts: 5 at a time (prevent rate limits)            │
│  • For each feed (AFS, Compado, Ads.com):                       │
│    - Fetch Google Ads data for TODAY only                       │
│    - Extract cost metrics (clicks, cost, impressions)           │
│    - Store in memory buffer                                      │
└─────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
              ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  STEP 3: Fetch Revenue Data (1-3 minutes)                       │
│  • AFS: Fetch AdSense revenue by style_id                       │
│  • Compado: Fetch conversions by GCLID                          │
│  • Ads.com: Fetch article performance                           │
│  • Store in memory buffer                                        │
└─────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
              ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  STEP 4: Save to MongoDB (30-60 seconds)                        │
│  • Use bulkWrite with upsert (prevent duplicates)               │
│  • Batch size: 1000 documents per write                         │
│  • Error handling: Log failures, continue with others           │
│  • Update sync_status collection                                │
└─────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
              ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  STEP 5: Update Redis Cache (10-20 seconds)                     │
│  • Cache today's aggregated data                                │
│  • Cache yesterday's data (if not already cached)               │
│  • Set TTL: 15 minutes                                          │
│  • Clear stale cache entries                                    │
└─────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
              ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  STEP 6: Health Check & Metrics (5 seconds)                     │
│  • Update sync_history                                          │
│  • Log success/failure metrics                                  │
│  • Respond to health check endpoint                             │
│  • Wait 15 minutes for next cycle                               │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

**Total Time per Cycle:** 3-8 minutes (well under 10-minute timeout)

